{# Telephone: flag + dial prefix, then the national number. Matches the
   client's Tally form.

   THE SELECT IS A REAL <select>, VISUALLY HIDDEN OVER THE DISPLAY.

   A custom listbox would need 246 <li role="option"> per form — about 22KB of
   markup on each of two pages — plus arrow-key handling, typeahead, focus
   trapping and a scroll-into-view, all of which a native select already does
   correctly and which mobile renders as its own wheel picker.

   So: the flag and dial code are a presentational display, and a transparent
   native select sits over the whole control. Clicking anywhere opens the
   platform picker; typing jumps by country name because the option text leads
   with the name. phone.js swaps the flag and dial text on change.

   Without JS the select still submits `phoneCountry` and the number still
   submits `phone`; only the flag stops updating, which loses nothing.

   Caller sets: fieldId, fieldRequired. Reads `countries` and `flags`.

   The sprite row index is emitted as data-row by the TEMPLATE, which already
   has the data at build time. The alternative was 246 CSS rules (~11KB against
   a 30KB budget) or a runtime lookup table; this costs ~10 bytes per option
   and needs neither. phone.js turns the row into a background-position via
   CSSOM, which CSP permits — it only blocks inline style attributes. #}
<div class="form__row form__row--full">
  <label class="label" for="{{ fieldId }}">Mobile number (with country code){% if fieldRequired %} <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>{% endif %}</label>
  <div class="phone">
    <span class="phone__country" data-phone-country>
      <span class="flag" data-flag-row="{{ flags.index[countries.default] }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="phone__dial" data-phone-dial>{{ countries.defaultDial }}</span>
      <svg class="phone__chev" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="14" height="14" fill="none"
           stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
           stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      <select class="phone__select" id="{{ fieldId }}-code" name="phoneCountry"
              aria-label="Country dialling code" autocomplete="tel-country-code">
        {% for c in countries.list %}
        <option value="+{{ c.dial }}" data-code="{{ c.code }}" data-row="{{ flags.index[c.code] }}"{% if c.code == countries.default %} selected{% endif %}>{{ c.name }} +{{ c.dial }}</option>
        {% endfor %}
      </select>
    </span>
    <input class="input phone__number" id="{{ fieldId }}" name="phone" type="tel"
           inputmode="tel" autocomplete="tel-national" enterkeyhint="next"
           maxlength="20" placeholder="712 345 678"
           aria-describedby="{{ fieldId }}-hint"{% if fieldRequired %} required{% endif %}>
  </div>
  <span class="form__hint" id="{{ fieldId }}-hint">Without the leading zero.</span>
</div>
